.Dd June 1, 2026
.Dt LIBSERVICE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm service_init ,
.Nm service_ready ,
.Nm service_register ,
.Nm service_unregister ,
.Nm service_lookup ,
.Nm service_accept ,
.Nm service_send ,
.Nm service_recv ,
.Nm service_channel_fd ,
.Nm service_protect
.Nd client library for services managed by serviced
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libservice
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In libservice.h
.Ft int
.Fn service_init void
.Ft int
.Fn service_ready void
.Ft int
.Fn service_register "const char *name"
.Ft int
.Fn service_unregister "const char *name"
.Ft int
.Fn service_lookup "const char *name"
.Ft int
.Fn service_accept "char *client_label" "size_t labelsz"
.Ft int
.Fn service_send "int fd" "const void *data" "size_t len"
.Ft ssize_t
.Fn service_recv "int fd" "void *buf" "size_t bufsz" "int *peer_fd"
.Ft int
.Fn service_channel_fd void
.Ft int
.Fn service_protect "uint32_t flags"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm libservice
library provides a clean API for services managed by
.Xr serviced 8
to communicate with the service manager over their inherited
mac_capability pair channel.
Services link against
.Nm libservice
and never need to include mac_capability headers or issue ioctls directly.
.Pp
.Fn service_init
initializes the library by reading the
.Ev ORACLED_CHANNEL_FD
environment variable to obtain the pair file descriptor
inherited from
.Xr serviced 8 .
This function must be called before any other function in the
library.
.Pp
.Fn service_ready
reports readiness to
.Xr serviced 8 .
This notifies the service manager that the service has completed
initialization and is ready to serve requests.
.Pp
.Fn service_register
registers a reverse-domain name
.Fa name
(e.g.,
.Dq org.5bsd.sshd )
with the
.Xr serviced 8
naming registry.
After registration, other services can connect via
.Fn service_lookup .
The name must contain at least one dot, consist only of
alphanumerics, dots, hyphens, and underscores, and must not
exceed 255 characters.
.Pp
.Fn service_unregister
removes a previously registered name from the naming registry.
Only the service that registered the name may remove it.
.Pp
.Fn service_lookup
connects to a named service by requesting a brokered connection
from
.Xr serviced 8 .
The service manager creates a new mac_capability pair, pushes one end
to the provider and returns the other end to the caller.
On success, a file descriptor for the bidirectional pair endpoint
is returned.
.Pp
.Fn service_accept
blocks until a client connects to one of this service's
registered names via
.Fn service_lookup .
On success, a file descriptor for the client connection is
returned.
If
.Fa client_label
is not
.Dv NULL ,
the connecting service's label is copied into it, up to
.Fa labelsz
bytes.
Notifications that arrive during an in-progress RPC are queued
internally and delivered from subsequent calls to
.Fn service_accept .
.Pp
.Fn service_send
sends a message on an arbitrary mac_capability pair file descriptor
.Fa fd .
This is a convenience wrapper around the
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_SENDMSG
ioctl.
.Pp
.Fn service_recv
receives a message from a mac_capability pair file descriptor
.Fa fd .
Up to
.Fa bufsz
bytes are read into
.Fa buf .
If
.Fa peer_fd
is not
.Dv NULL
and the message carries an attached file descriptor, it is
stored in
.Fa *peer_fd ;
otherwise
.Fa *peer_fd
is set to \-1.
This is a convenience wrapper around the
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_RECVMSG
ioctl.
.Pp
.Fn service_channel_fd
returns the pair file descriptor to
.Xr serviced 8
that was established during
.Fn service_init .
This is useful for registering the fd with
.Xr kqueue 2
for event-driven services.
Returns \-1 if the library has not been initialized.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn service_init ,
.Fn service_ready ,
.Fn service_register ,
.Fn service_unregister ,
and
.Fn service_send
return 0 on success and \-1 on failure, setting
.Va errno .
.Pp
.Fn service_lookup
and
.Fn service_accept
return a non-negative file descriptor on success and \-1 on
failure, setting
.Va errno .
.Pp
.Fn service_recv
returns the number of bytes received on success and \-1 on
failure, setting
.Va errno .
.Pp
.Fn service_channel_fd
returns the pair file descriptor, or \-1 if the library has not
been initialized.
.Pp
.Fn service_protect
applies
.Xr mac_capability_capprotect 4
shielding to the calling service using the
.Ev ORACLED_CAPPROTECT_FD
descriptor inherited from
.Xr serviced 8 .
The
.Fa flags
argument is a
.Dv CP_SF_*
bitmask; 0 requests the capprotect default.
It returns 0 on success, or \-1 on failure with
.Va errno
set.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Basic provider pattern:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <libservice.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int
main(void)
{
    char label[64];
    int client_fd;

    if (service_init() == -1)
        return (1);

    service_ready();
    service_register("org.example.myservice");

    for (;;) {
        client_fd = service_accept(label, sizeof(label));
        if (client_fd == -1)
            break;
        printf("client connected: %s\\n", label);
        /* handle client_fd ... */
    }

    service_unregister("org.example.myservice");
    return (0);
}
.Ed
.Pp
Basic client pattern:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <libservice.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int
main(void)
{
    int peer;
    char buf[256];
    ssize_t n;

    if (service_init() == -1)
        return (1);

    service_ready();

    peer = service_lookup("org.example.myservice");
    if (peer == -1)
        return (1);

    service_send(peer, "hello", 5);
    n = service_recv(peer, buf, sizeof(buf), NULL);
    if (n > 0)
        printf("received %zd bytes\\n", n);

    return (0);
}
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
The following errors are common to multiple functions:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er ENOTCONN
The library has not been initialized via
.Fn service_init ,
or the pair fd has become invalid.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
An invalid argument was passed (e.g., a malformed name).
.El
.Pp
.Fn service_init
may fail with:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er ENOENT
The
.Ev ORACLED_CHANNEL_FD
environment variable is not set.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The value of
.Ev ORACLED_CHANNEL_FD
is not a valid file descriptor number.
.El
.Pp
.Fn service_register
may fail with:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er ENAMETOOLONG
The name exceeds 255 characters.
.It Bq Er EEXIST
The name is already registered by another service.
.It Bq Er ENOSPC
The service has reached its per-service registration limit (32).
.El
.Pp
.Fn service_unregister
may fail with:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er ENAMETOOLONG
The name exceeds 255 characters.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
The name is not registered.
.It Bq Er EPERM
The name is registered by a different service.
.El
.Pp
.Fn service_lookup
may fail with:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er ENAMETOOLONG
The name exceeds 255 characters.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
The name is not registered.
.It Bq Er ELOOP
The caller attempted to connect to itself.
.It Bq Er ECONNRESET
The provider's pair channel has closed.
.It Bq Er EDEADLK
An on-demand circular dependency was detected
(the provider requires a service that the caller provides).
.It Bq Er ETIMEDOUT
The lookup RPC did not complete within the internal timeout
(100 ms).
This can occur if the provider is being launched on-demand
and has not yet registered.
.It Bq Er EIO
Failed to create a pair or notify the provider.
.El
.Sh CAVEATS
The library is not thread-safe.
The internal pair fd and notification queue are stored in static
variables; concurrent access from multiple threads will produce
undefined behavior.
.Pp
The library is not safe to use across
.Xr fork 2
without a subsequent
.Xr execve 2 .
The pair fd is shared between parent and child after fork, and
interleaved messages will corrupt protocol state.
.Pp
.Fn service_accept
blocks on the pair fd.
If the service needs to multiplex the pair fd with other event
sources, use
.Fn service_channel_fd
to obtain the fd and register it with
.Xr kqueue 2
or
.Xr poll 2 ,
then call
.Fn service_accept
only when the fd is readable.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
.Xr serviced 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm libservice
first appeared in 5BSD.
